# IMP-07 (D-3, REQ-004, AC-006 web part; ARCH-REV-002 N-1) every row time is the node's: the pre-D-3 web, then the fix
# command: cd autobyteus-web && NUXT_TEST=true pnpm exec vitest run --reporter=verbose services/agentStreaming/__tests__/serverRowTimes.spec.ts
#          (first with the 22 pre-D-3 web source files from HEAD b45ef33694 checked out, the D-3 files restored after)
# commit: b45ef33694 web source (pre-D-3, with D-1 and D-2); 87d7321915 (fix)
# env: macOS arm64, Node v22.23.1; the viewer's clock by fake timers, 2 s behind and 2 s ahead; frame times on odd ms
# date: 2026-11-23
# result: Reproduced, then fixed. Pre-D-3 all 4 fail: the own send carries the viewer's clock (16:55:07 behind, 16:55:11
#   ahead) and a frame without a time is accepted. With D-3 all 4 pass: the own send is null until the echo's received_at
#   (Team) or the input state's accepted_at (standalone, N-1; a later revision keeps the time shown); the notice, agent
#   message, tool Activity row and compaction row carry their frames' occurred_at; updatedAt is the latest row time; a
#   frame without occurred_at is refused at the parser.

